13:- Optional `keys.resize_pane_left`, `keys.resize_pane_down`, `keys.resize_pane_up`, and `keys.resize_pane_right` bindings now resize the focused pane in one keystroke without entering resize mode. (#2558, thanks @dhh)
28:- Experimental pane graphics now support bounded named layers, acknowledged full-RGBA primary-layer direct file frames on audited local terminals, owned BGRA fallback, exact pixel mouse input, and placement-only resize replay.
50:- `prefix+e` now preserves logical lines when opening soft-wrapped scrollback in an editor. (#2733)
163:- Clients repaint after transient terminal resizes instead of leaving stale or missing rows.
211:- Pane viewports that were following live output now continue following after a resize.
281:- Added `layout.updated` socket events so protocol clients can keep tab layout snapshots current after pane split, resize, swap, move, zoom, and layout mutations.
284:- Added `herdr terminal session control` for bridge processes that need live ANSI frames plus input, resize, scroll, release, and takeover authority.
305:- Plain PageUp/PageDown now reach primary-screen pager apps such as `less -X` and Git diff when they enter application cursor mode, while shell transcripts still use Herdr pane scrollback. (#953)
307:- `prefix+e` scrollback editor panes now open on Windows without trying to run `/bin/sh`; Windows uses `VISUAL`, then `EDITOR`, then `notepad.exe` as the fallback editor. (#914)
349:- Windows Terminal multiline text paste now reaches pane apps as one bracketed paste, so OMP, Pi, and similar prompts no longer submit each pasted line separately. Plain Esc, Shift+Enter, mouse, focus, resize, and Unicode paste handling are preserved on the Windows client path. (#670)
391:- Pane resize keybindings now shrink panes again instead of only being able to grow them. (#562)
414:- Codex blocker detection now ignores stale prompt text outside the live prompt region, reducing false blocked states from old scrollback.
420:- Resizing restored panes no longer aborts the server when libghostty-vt reflows a terminal whose pre-resize cursor row is past the new height. (#465)
421:- Full-screen TUIs such as Neovim now receive resize-generated terminal responses after Herdr internal pane resizes, so grown panes redraw without waiting for extra input. (#471)
423:- Headless servers now avoid repeated scrollback rendering work for inactive panes, reducing CPU in large sessions. (#512)
436:- Added directional pane swap with `prefix+shift+h/j/k/l`, a pane context-menu swap action, pane layout/neighbor/edge/focus/resize socket APIs, matching CLI commands, and optional `pane split --ratio` support. (#330, #421)
479:- Claude Code background-agent wait text in scrollback no longer keeps an idle pane marked working after the background agent has completed.
541:- Added scrollback support to direct agent terminal attaches. Mouse wheel and plain PageUp/PageDown now scroll the attached terminal viewport, while terminal apps that request mouse or alternate-scroll input still receive those events. The client/server protocol is now version 11.
578:- Added `ui.mouse_scroll_lines` to configure how many pane scrollback lines each mouse wheel notch scrolls. The default remains 3. (#236)
634:- Added `ui.sidebar_min_width` and `ui.sidebar_max_width` to configure the sidebar's expanded resize bounds. Defaults remain 18 and 36 columns; existing configs are unchanged. (#132, #135, thanks @ChihGodlee)
660:- Added optional `keys.edit_scrollback` to open the focused pane's retained scrollback in `$EDITOR` inside a temporary zoomed pane. (#122)
671:- Split pane resize hit areas no longer overlap the first content column or row, making text selection work from the start of right and bottom panes. (#120)
672:- Dragging text selections near pane edges now autoscrolls into scrollback, and selection state now clears correctly when switching workspaces, tabs, or panes. (#128, #129, thanks @leeeanh)
687:- PageUp and PageDown now scroll Herdr pane scrollback for normal panes while still forwarding keys to full-screen or mouse-reporting apps.
710:- Background tabs now resize when the outer terminal size changes, preventing stale pane dimensions when switching back to them.
